{
  "case_id": "2016-16-466",
  "document_hash": "683eb00c0f04c4806dc7d213a9e25146827e6b39f8913db6056acc28fce3f40d",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2016-16-466",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "683eb00c0f04c4806dc7d213a9e25146827e6b39f8913db6056acc28fce3f40d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-683eb00c0f04-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:08 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Neal K. Katyal",
      "case_id": "2016-16-466",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "683eb00c0f04c4806dc7d213a9e25146827e6b39f8913db6056acc28fce3f40d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-683eb00c0f04-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The California Supreme Court ruled that hundreds of plaintiffs who were not prescribed a drug in California, who did not take it in California, who lacked any injury in California, and who had no other connection to California could sue in California."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Neal K. Katyal",
      "case_id": "2016-16-466",
      "confidence": 0.92,
      "document_hash": "683eb00c0f04c4806dc7d213a9e25146827e6b39f8913db6056acc28fce3f40d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-683eb00c0f04-0000-0003",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Instead of achieving jurisdictional fairness, their rule would distribute their burden of defending mass torts in a lopsided way."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2016-16-466",
      "confidence": 0.93,
      "document_hash": "683eb00c0f04c4806dc7d213a9e25146827e6b39f8913db6056acc28fce3f40d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-683eb00c0f04-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If -- if this suit went forward just with the California plaintiffs and Bristol-Myers did not prevail, would there be issue preclusion in other States, assuming that judgment was final?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2016-16-466",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "683eb00c0f04c4806dc7d213a9e25146827e6b39f8913db6056acc28fce3f40d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-683eb00c0f04-0000-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 11,
        "start": 11
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There are 575 out-of-State plaintiffs from 33 States."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2016-16-466",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "683eb00c0f04c4806dc7d213a9e25146827e6b39f8913db6056acc28fce3f40d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-683eb00c0f04-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: But if this were -- if this were a case where the nonresident plaintiffs were Alderson Reporting Company"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2016-16-466",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "683eb00c0f04c4806dc7d213a9e25146827e6b39f8913db6056acc28fce3f40d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-683eb00c0f04-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: There is an amicus brief here that talked about all of the criminal laws that would be subject to questioning under your theory of -- of constitutional due process."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Goldstein",
      "case_id": "2016-16-466",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "683eb00c0f04c4806dc7d213a9e25146827e6b39f8913db6056acc28fce3f40d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-683eb00c0f04-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "that, I think, is what -- I think that's what they're saying is the special federalism interest of either the home State or the State where they did the manufacturing, or the State where they, you know, whatever the other one is where you count as a home State. That does sound special."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2016-16-466",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "683eb00c0f04c4806dc7d213a9e25146827e6b39f8913db6056acc28fce3f40d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-683eb00c0f04-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And on that, I just wonder if -- if we move to this all-things-considered approach, are we collapsing what had been previously two separate due process inquiries, one was purposeful availment, and the other was fundamental fairness. And as I hear it, really, it all just boils down to fundamental fairness."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2016-16-466",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "683eb00c0f04c4806dc7d213a9e25146827e6b39f8913db6056acc28fce3f40d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-683eb00c0f04-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So I'm just wondering what happens doctrinally to the first test? Does it have any bite?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Goldstein",
      "case_id": "2016-16-466",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "683eb00c0f04c4806dc7d213a9e25146827e6b39f8913db6056acc28fce3f40d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-683eb00c0f04-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "California court is providing a forum to adjudicate a claim about the lawfulness of BMS's design and manufacturing and distribution of this drug Plavix. That is activity that didn't occur in California. Okay? That is activity that they quite clearly say happened in New Jersey."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2016-16-466",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "683eb00c0f04c4806dc7d213a9e25146827e6b39f8913db6056acc28fce3f40d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-683eb00c0f04-0002-0009",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "California court is providing a forum to adjudicate a claim about the lawfulness of BMS's design and manufacturing and distribution of this drug Plavix."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2016-16-466",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "683eb00c0f04c4806dc7d213a9e25146827e6b39f8913db6056acc28fce3f40d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-683eb00c0f04-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In the State court or the Southern District?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2016-16-466",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "683eb00c0f04c4806dc7d213a9e25146827e6b39f8913db6056acc28fce3f40d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-683eb00c0f04-0002-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Goldstein, it seems to me, on your theory, it could be zero California plaintiffs, because here's what you told me. You told me that the reason that this -- that an Ohio citizen's claim arises out of the contacts in California is because the contacts in California are really nationwide contacts. And if that's so, it's met regardless of whether there are any California plaintiffs are not."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2016-16-466",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "683eb00c0f04c4806dc7d213a9e25146827e6b39f8913db6056acc28fce3f40d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-683eb00c0f04-0002-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What's left?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2016-16-466",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "683eb00c0f04c4806dc7d213a9e25146827e6b39f8913db6056acc28fce3f40d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-683eb00c0f04-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: But why am I here in respect to Smith? Because, you see, Smith isn't a citizen of our State."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Goldstein",
      "case_id": "2016-16-466",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "683eb00c0f04c4806dc7d213a9e25146827e6b39f8913db6056acc28fce3f40d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-683eb00c0f04-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. GOLDSTEIN: All right. Well, all I will tell you is this point about nonmutual offensive collateral estoppel is a big deal. And that is when you have the identical claim, identical legal theory, identical operative facts, it -- so take away all of his it's all very different, the premise of this case is that it's all the same."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2016-16-466",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "683eb00c0f04c4806dc7d213a9e25146827e6b39f8913db6056acc28fce3f40d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-683eb00c0f04-0003-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the -- the -- an important part of our analysis is that there is the governmental interest in that the litigation in this forum does consolidate things and make it simpler. The State's interest in having 600 cases litigated together rather than in 50 different forums, it's material to our case that it does simplify things."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2016-16-466",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "683eb00c0f04c4806dc7d213a9e25146827e6b39f8913db6056acc28fce3f40d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-683eb00c0f04-0003-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 64,
        "start": 64
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2016-16-466",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "683eb00c0f04c4806dc7d213a9e25146827e6b39f8913db6056acc28fce3f40d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-683eb00c0f04-0003-0004",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 64,
        "start": 64
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And the predictability here is incredibly important."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2016-16-466",
      "confidence": 0.0,
